Z||000005||DecadenceR||07-05-2001||01:12 AM||||The prowler I kinda like. To me, it's one of those things, you can't really figure out if you like it or hate it. I do think it's over rated and over priced though. As for the P/T, that was never worth the effort.<BR>But the Liberty is just God Awful Ugly!!! You look at the Grand Cherokee, and how nice that is. You'd think they would have better taste than this...<BR>BTW, since when is Jeep no longer making the Cherokee? Just the Grand Cherokee? I know Honda is discontinuing the Prelude and marketing a hybrid Civic, but I don't remember hearing about the Cherokee...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||07-05-2001||02:16 AM||||Yeah it looks like a cartoonish version of an old Jeep. But it seems to be built to actually go offroad. Maybe that was the plan, make them so bad looking that people will willingly drive them away from civilizaton.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||07-05-2001||06:32 AM||||They were designed with the off roader in mind, but most "off road" vehicles never see anything but pavement.  I think they look like a Kia Sportage.  (gag)  Here's the way I see it.  You want a capable off road vehicle that you can still drive around town, to the movies, pick up the kids (might be a bad example here) and have 30 grand to spend?  You can either buy a new Liberty or a 5 year old Hummer.  My choice is the Hummer (although you'd think, for 70 grand new, they'd have more seating capacity).  Actually, I could live the rest of my life with just 3 vehicles.  My Fiero, my bike and a Hummer.  Hmmm...What's the penalty for robbing a bank?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
