Z||000015||Rex||07-06-2001||07:20 PM||||The Kia Sportage is terrible, and prssibly one of the worst SUVs made.<P>just wondering DecadenceR what you are basing that on? No I don't own one but am considering looking at one.I do know they have a frame unlike the Honda SUV and the Santa fee. would be nice if they had a v-6 option to go with that 10-year warranty||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cheever2||07-06-2001||09:58 PM||||My wife informed me about this topic, so I came slummin' into the O/T section to enlighten you regarding the Jeep Liberty.  She and I each got to drive Liberty's through some <B>very</B> rough terrain.  I did some serious offroad 4-wheeling for several years and I know what qualifies a vehicle as a respectable offroader.  Let me tell you, the Liberty is a <B>serious</B> offroad machine!  It did some amazing things, and I was grinning from ear to ear when I got out of it.  And not only that, but it was roomier and more comfortable than a Grand Cherokee, and that's as much a matter of opinion as the former statements, but I would LOVE to have one, now that I have driven it.  Give it a chance.  Check it out.  Tell em Cheever2 sent ya, it won't get you a discount, but they would look at ya kinda funny.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000017||DecadenceR||07-07-2001||12:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rex:<BR><B>The Kia Sportage is terrible, and prssibly one of the worst SUVs made.<P>just wondering DecadenceR what you are basing that on? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Rex, I used to sell cars. As we all know, one of the benifits of that is being able to drive the cars. While working at the dealership, I personally brought in 3 of them as a trade in. One of which the woman traded in 2 weeks after buying it. Triving them they feel very tipsy, like you're going to flip when you turn the next corner. The rear latches for the spare tire often get stuck, don't work, and need to be replaced. And as for that 10 year warranty, you will be using it quite often. They habitually break down. And for a new car, you;d think it'd be a little more reliable.<BR>As for the Honda SUV, they are only overpriced Isuzu Rodeos. Isuzu actually makes them for Honda, and Honda slaps their labels on them. VERY good vehicles though. i'd LOVE a Rodeo.<BR>If you want a SUV with a full frame instead of a body bolted onto a frame, the Suzuki Grand Vitara are pretty good, definitely better than the KIA. They are Unibody, they come V-6 and if I remember right you can get the v6 in a 5speed. They also have a 10 year warranty and unlike the kia, they have a steel self adjusting timing chain. <BR>If you haven't looked at it yet, I also suggest looking at the Mazda Tribute. Althouth, everyone has them. I LOVED that thing. $27000 gets you a V6 auto with power everything, sunroof, leather, tow package...<BR>Anyway, everyone's tastes are different, so good luck.||||reg||1
